      "narration": "Now panes. Backslash splits the editor, so you can read one file while writing another. The number one returns you to the first pane. W closes an editor — and here's the one nobody knows: shift with T reopens whatever you just closed. Closing stops being destructive once you can undo it, which changes how freely you do it.",
      "data": {
